  "reason": "Evidence: The largest performance jump in the study is from single-profile to multi-profile in the multimodal setting (0.53→0.725), while RNA-only single-profile (scvi_n200) achieves 0.52 and image-only is negligible (~0.21). We have not yet tested whether the multi-profile + transformer aggregation gain is specific to the multimodal interaction or is a general property of aggregating multiple RNA profiles. Question: config_007 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) directly tests whether multi-profile aggregation alone, without any image modality, can reproduce the large accuracy gain. Why this is the best next experiment: If RNA-only multi-profile also jumps toward ~0.70, the gain is driven by RNA profile aggregation and the image contributes less than assumed, redirecting effort toward better RNA aggregation. If it stays near 0.52, the multi-profile gain is specifically a multimodal interaction effect, confirming that image+RNA synergy is essential and justifying continued investment in multimodal multi-profile configurations. This single experiment resolves a high-uncertainty mechanistic question that would significantly reshape the remaining search strategy, making it more informative than a small incremental fusion-type or encoder swap on the already-strong multimodal multi-profile setting."
}

